--   **The copy on managed states.**
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.R6MCpy`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem IntMul.Kappa.R6.cpyD_sp {Z X : Fin HS} (hZX : Z ≠ X) (hZ5 : Z.val < 56) (hX5 : X.val < 56)
--       (hZy : Z ≠ yC) (hZc : Z ≠ cC) (hXy : X ≠ yC) (hXc : X ≠ cC) (hXd : X ≠ zDd) (hZd : Z ≠ zDd)
--       (s : IState HS) (f : Fin HS → List ℤ) (desc : List ℤ) (hfZ : f Z = desc) (hfX : f X = [])
--       (hfY : f yC = []) (hfC : f cC = []) (hfD : f zDd = []) (k c dv B : ℕ)
--       (hdv : (encK s f).top zDd = dv) (hdi : (encK s f).IsInt zDd) (hlen : desc.length = k * dv + c)
--       (hB1 : k * dv + c < 2 ^ B) (hB2 : dv < 2 ^ B) (hB : Bnd B desc) :
--       Sp (cpyD Z X k c) (encK s f) (encK s (Function.update f X desc))
--         (2 * (2 * k + 2) * 2000 * (B + 2) + desc.length * (40000 * (B + 2) + 30) + 64)
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** Round-six machine: copying a stored descriptor
--
--   The setup leaves the descriptors of the interface calls on `zPh`, `zLn`, `zCh` (`BaseOK6`). Before
--   a call, `cpyD Z X k c` copies the `k d + c` integers on top of `Z` onto the builder stack `X`
--   and leaves `Z` as it was (`d` from `zDd`; scratch `40`, counter `41`):
--   `mvK Z 40 41 n` moves them to `40` reversed, then a counted loop pushes each one back on `Z` and
--   on `X`.
--
--   * **`cpyD_sp`**: the specification on managed states.
--   * **`cpyD_run`**: the form `callW_I` uses: from any state with the descriptor on top of `Z`.
